    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nqTox v1.18.4\n\n### Commit Hash\n\ne7878b6b689e7df71b93876d5fc59775756c4c76\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Qt Version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Activate Make Tox Portable option\n3. Close qTox\n4. Reopen qTox\n\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nMake Tox Portable option not working properly. On latest flatpak version and latest apt version qTox \"Make Tox Portable\" option is not working, in the app logs it shows there is an error with the file lock and in the filesystem, the file is never saved in the new location. When reopening the app, the change has no effect and it has default configuration\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nMake Tox portable option should save the profile files in the location shown in the app logs\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nLinux\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nUbuntu 24.04 LTS\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
